{"id":"word:hebrew:H7198","type":"word","title":"קֶשֶׁת","subtitle":"H7198 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a bow , for shooting (hence, figuratively, strength ) or the iris","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to קֶשֶׁת (H7198) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 76 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"קֶשֶׁת (qesheth) means a bow , for shooting (hence, figuratively, strength ) or the iris First listed occurrence: 1Chr 5 18."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"קֶשֶׁת","transliteration":"qesheth","pronunciation":"keh'-sheth","strong":"H7198","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7198","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["קֶ֣שֶׁת","קֶ֔שֶׁת","קֶ֗שֶׁת","קָ֑שֶׁת","בַּ/קָּ֑שֶׁת"],"morphs":[["HNcfsa",24],["HNcfsc",9],["HNcfsc/Sp3ms",7],["HRd/Ncfsa",6],["HTd/Ncfsa",5],["HR/Ncfsa",3],["HC/Ncfpa",2],["HNcfsc/Sp2ms",2],["HR/Ncfsc",2],["HNcfsc/Sp3mp",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"a bow , for shooting (hence, figuratively, strength ) or the iris","usage":"× arch(-er), arrow, bow(-man, -shot).","full":"H7198. qesheth קֶ֫שֶׁת noun feminine Gen 9:14 (apparently masculine 2Sam 1:22 but see Albr ZAW xvi (1896) 91 ) bow (originally √ perhaps קושׁ , meaning unknown; Late Hebrew id. ; Assyrian ‡aštu ; Ethiopic Arabic plural , etc.; ᵑ7 and ( קַשְׁתָּא and ( ט for ת after ק P) קוּשְׁטָא (rare), all bow , קַשָּׁתָא bowman ; Syriac bow , bowman ; Old Aramaic קשת bow , Mandean כשטא (Frä 206 ); Palmyrene קשטא bowman ); — absolute ׳ק Hosea 1:7 +, קָ֑שֶׁת Jer 46:9 +; construct קֶ֫שֶׁת Hosea 1:5 +; suffix קַשְׁתִּי Gen 48:22 + ,etc.; plural absolute קְשָׁתוֺת 2Chr 26:14 +; suffix קַשְּׁתֹתָיו (Ges § 20h ) Isa 5:28 , קַשְּׁתוֺתָם Jer 51:56 ; Psa 37:15 , קַשְּׁתֹתֵיהֶם Neh 4:7 ( קַשְׁתֹּתָיו etc., van d. H. [except Psa 37:15 ]); &#8212; 1 bow : a. for hunting Gen 27:3 (J; + תְּלְי ) b. battle: + (or ||) חֶרֶב Gen 48:22 ; Josh 24:12 (both E), Hosea 1:7 ; 2:20 ; 1Sam 18:4 (+ חְַגֹרוֺ ), 2Sam 1:22 ; 2Kin 6:22 ; Isa 41:2 ; Neh 4:7 (+ רָמְחֵיהֶם ), Zech 9:13 (figurative of Judah as ׳י s bow), Psa 37:15 (figurative) 44:7 (+ or || חֶרֶב also below) ;+ (or ||) חִצִּים Isa 7:24 ; 2Kin 13:15 (twice in verse); Ezek 39:3 , 9 ; 1Chr 12:2 a; compare ק ׳רִשְׁפֵי Psa 76:4 = arrow (+ וְחֶרֶב מָנֵן ) so ק ׳בֶּן Job 41:20 (compare Lam 3:13 ; Job 5:7 ); + חֲנִית Psa 46:10 , + כִּידוֺן Jer 6:23 ; 50:42 ; + varius weapons Neh 4:10 ; 2Chr 26:14 ; alone Isa 13:18 (context corrupt), 22:3 ; Jer 51:56 ; Hab 3:9 (of ׳י as warrior ); ׳ק מִלְחָמָה Zech 9:10 ; 10:4 ; in simile ׳כְּק רְמִיָּה like a bow of deception Hosea 7:16 ; Psa 78:57 (i.e. one that misses its aim; al. slack bow ). c. ׳ק collective = bow (-men), archers Isa 21:17 . d. phrases are: בַּקּ אֲנָשִׁים ׳הַמּרִים 1Sam 31:3 archers, bowmen (but dubious; Dr Kit Löhr translates, ׳א ׳הַמּ ; We Bu strike out ׳א as || 1Chr 10:3 ; HPS Now strike out ׳א ׳בַּקּ ), בַּקּ ׳הַמּוֺרִים 10:3 ; ק ׳מְטַחֲוֵי Gen 21:16 (see [ טָתָה ], ק ׳רמֵה Jer 4:29 , compare perhaps Gen 21:21 see קִשָּׁת , || ק ׳נשְׁקֵי (see II. נָשַׁק ) 1Chr 12:2 b 2Chr 17:17 , ׳נוֺ ק ׳רוֺמֵי Psa 78:9 ; הַקּ ׳תֹּפֵשׁ Amos 2:15 one grasping the bow , (see Jer 46:9 below) see also בַקּ יָדוֺ ׳מִלֵּא 2Kin 9:24 , עַלהַֿקּ יָֽדְךָ ׳הַרְכֵּב 13:16 ; ק ׳דָּרַח bend (literally tread ) the bow , Isa 5:28 (participle passive), 21:15 ( id. ; || חֶרֶב ) Jer 50:14 , 29 ; 51:3 ; 1Chr 5:18 ; 8:40 ; 2Chr 14:7 ; Psa 37:14 (|| חֶרֶב ), in figure 11:2 (|| חֵץ ), and, of God, Lam 2:4 ; 3:12 ; Psa 7:13 (|| הֶרֶב ); ק דֹּרְכֵי ׳תֹּפְשֵׂי Jer 46:9 ; compare(figurative) קַשְׁתָּם אֶתלְֿשׁוֺנָם וַיַּדְרְכוֺ 9:2 ; also ׳ק וְנִחֲתָה נְחוּשָׁה Psa 18:35 = 2Sam 22:35 (read וְנִחֲתָה for וְנִחַת ) בַּקּ ׳מָשַׁח draw the bow 1Kin 22:34 2Chr 18:33 ; Isa 66:19 . e. bow (passing over into) figurative of might Gen 49:24 (poem), 1Sam 2:4 ; Hosea 1:5 ; Jer 49:35 ; Job 29:20 (compare Psa 37:15 , b. above) feminine ׳ק נְחוּשָׁה fig of divine judgment Job 20:24 (|| בַּרְזֶל נֵשֶׁק ) 2 rainbow : הַקּ ׳כְּמַר